WEBVTT

00:00:00.246 --> 00:00:01.040
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 4

00:00:02.032 --> 00:00:05.336
Idioms and expressions with measurements

00:00:05.875 --> 00:00:06.653
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 1

00:00:07.447 --> 00:00:10.261
<v><b>F:</b></v> Sam thought he’d get away with not doing his coursework,

00:00:10.285 --> 00:00:13.125
but his tutor came down on him like a ton of bricks.

00:00:14.993 --> 00:00:15.676
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 2

00:00:16.517 --> 00:00:21.626
<v><b>M:</b></v> When the tanker sank, gallons of oil washed ashore and thousands of seabirds died.

00:00:23.557 --> 00:00:24.319
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 3

00:00:25.125 --> 00:00:30.413
<v><b>M:</b></v> Whatever you do, don’t mention moving in together on your first date, or she’ll run a mile.

00:00:32.262 --> 00:00:33.084
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 4

00:00:33.981 --> 00:00:37.835
<v><b>F:</b></v> Can you give me a hand with this huge box? It weighs a ton.

00:00:39.740 --> 00:00:40.602
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 5

00:00:41.419 --> 00:00:46.495
<v><b>M:</b></v> Fiona’s so conscientious. She’ll always go the extra mile to complete a project on time.

00:00:48.376 --> 00:00:49.259
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 6

00:00:50.037 --> 00:00:52.414
<v><b>F:</b></v> I had a narrow escape this morning

00:00:52.415 --> 00:00:58.039
– a great chunk fell off the cliff as I was walking on the beach. It missed me by inches!

00:00:59.887 --> 00:01:00.757
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 7

00:01:01.559 --> 00:01:06.763
<v><b>A:</b></v> I lent him my bike just for the weekend, and two weeks later, I still haven’t got it back!

00:01:06.970 --> 00:01:10.327
<v><b>B:</b></v> I did warn you! Give him an inch and he’ll take a mile.

00:01:12.181 --> 00:01:12.848
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 8

00:01:13.792 --> 00:01:15.798
<v><b>M:</b></v> We’re going to be really late

00:01:15.869 --> 00:01:21.636
– it’s 11.30 already and thanks to that accident on the motorway, we’re still miles away.

00:01:23.499 --> 00:01:24.353
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 9

00:01:25.187 --> 00:01:30.193
<v><b>F:</b></v> I know he promised you half the house, but I wouldn’t trust him an inch, if I were you.

00:01:32.145 --> 00:01:32.828
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 10

00:01:33.471 --> 00:01:37.638
<v><b>M:</b></v> On my first day in the job, I wore a suit, but I stood out a mile

00:01:37.883 --> 00:01:39.978
– everyone else was in jeans and T- shirts.